1. Keep `BXtoKst` as a small domain model that only stores values and exposes basic getters/setters.
2. Move arithmetic and currency conversion into a service such as `BXtoKstCalculator` or `BXtoKstOperations`.
3. Move comparison/reporting into a separate comparer/report generator.
4. Move XML writing into a serializer class.
5. Replace `IoC.Resolve<IBAfronden>()` with constructor injection.
6. Replace repeated loops over the matrix with helper methods to reduce duplication.

Example refactor:

```csharp
public sealed class BXtoKst
{
    private readonly double[,] _values = new double[(int)EXto.Atl, (int)EKst.StdAtl];

    public int Valuta { get; private set; }

    public double this[EXto xto, EKst kst]
    {
        get => _values[(int)xto, (int)kst];
        set => _values[(int)xto, (int)kst] = value;
    }

    public void SetValuta(int valuta) => Valuta = valuta;
}

public sealed class BXtoKstCalculator
{
    private readonly IBAfronden _afronden;
    private readonly IValutaConverter _converter;

    public BXtoKstCalculator(IBAfronden afronden, IValutaConverter converter)
    {
        _afronden = afronden;
        _converter = converter;
    }

    public void ConvertCurrency(BXtoKst target, int newValuta, IList<BValutaDeco> valutaVzl)
    {
        // conversion logic here
    }
}
```

This refactoring reduces coupling, improves testability, and makes each class easier to reason about and evolve independently.

